#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/filters/morphology.rst:2
msgid "Morphological operations"
msgstr "形態學運算"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/filters/morphology.rst:4
msgid ""
"*Morphological* operations work on binary images -- the masks that come out "
"of thresholding and edge detection. Each operation walks the same kind of "
"sliding neighbourhood the smoothing filters use, but the question it asks at"
" every position is yes/no: is *every* pixel in the neighbourhood on, is "
"*any* pixel in the neighbourhood on, what does the on/off pattern look like?"
" The answers grow regions, shrink them, and recut their boundaries in ways "
"an averaging filter cannot."
msgstr ""
"*形態學* "
"運算作用於二值影像——也就是閾值化與邊緣偵測所產生的遮罩。每個運算都會走過與平滑濾波器相同的那種滑動鄰域，但它在每個位置提出的問題是是/否：鄰域中的 "
"*每個* 像素都是開啟的嗎？鄰域中是否有 *任何* "
"像素是開啟的？開/關的圖樣看起來如何？這些答案能以平均濾波器辦不到的方式擴張區域、收縮區域，並重新切割它們的邊界。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/filters/morphology.rst:16
msgid ""
"Morphology is what comes between an *initial* binary mask -- the output of "
"thresholding, edge detection, or some other classifier -- and the *clean* "
"binary mask the rest of the pipeline can use. A raw threshold output usually"
" has isolated noise pixels scattered through true-foreground areas, small "
"holes punched into otherwise solid regions, and jagged boundaries where the "
"threshold cut close to the edge of an object. Morphology removes those "
"defects."
msgstr ""
"形態學介於 *初始* 二值遮罩（閾值化、邊緣偵測或其他分類器的輸出）與管線其餘部分可用的 *乾淨* "
"二值遮罩之間。原始的閾值輸出通常會有散佈在真正前景區域中的孤立雜訊像素、在原本完整的區域中打出的小孔洞，以及閾值切在物體邊緣附近時所產生的鋸齒狀邊界。形態學能去除這些缺陷。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/filters/morphology.rst:28
msgid "The four classical operations"
msgstr "四種經典運算"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/filters/morphology.rst:30
msgid ""
"Two primitive operations, and two compositions of them, make up the "
"morphological toolkit:"
msgstr "兩個基本運算，加上它們的兩種組合，構成了形態學工具組："

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/filters/morphology.rst:33
msgid ""
":meth:`~image.Image.dilate` *grows* every foreground region. The rule is: "
"any pixel that has at least one foreground neighbour in its ``(2 * size + "
"1)`` window becomes foreground. The visible effect is that foreground "
"regions get bigger by ``size`` pixels in every direction, and *holes* inside"
" them shrink (or disappear) by the same amount."
msgstr ""
":meth:`~image.Image.dilate` *擴張* 每個前景區域。其規則是：任何在其 ``(2 * size + 1)`` "
"視窗中至少有一個前景鄰居的像素都會變成前景。可見的效果是前景區域在每個方向上擴大 ``size`` 個像素，而其內部的 *孔洞* "
"則縮小（或消失）相同的量。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/filters/morphology.rst:42
msgid ""
":meth:`~image.Image.erode` does the inverse. Any pixel that does not have "
"*every* neighbour in its window in the foreground becomes background. "
"Foreground regions get smaller by ``size`` pixels in every direction, "
"isolated foreground pixels (which have no foreground neighbours) disappear "
"entirely, and small connections between larger regions get cut."
msgstr ""
":meth:`~image.Image.erode` 則相反。任何在其視窗中並非 *每個* 鄰居都屬於前景的像素都會變成背景。前景區域在每個方向上縮小 "
"``size`` 個像素，孤立的前景像素（沒有任何前景鄰居）完全消失，而較大區域之間的細小連接也會被切斷。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/filters/morphology.rst:51
msgid ""
"A binary input region in the leftmost\n"
"panel: a solid square with a one-pixel\n"
"hole in its middle and three isolated\n"
"noise pixels around it. Four panels to\n"
"the right show the result of applying\n"
"dilate, erode, open, and close to that\n"
"input. Dilate grows the region, fills\n"
"the hole, and grows each noise pixel\n"
"into a block; erode shrinks the region,\n"
"grows the hole, and removes the noise;\n"
"open removes the noise while\n"
"reproducing the region and its hole\n"
"exactly; close fills the hole while\n"
"reproducing the region's outline and\n"
"the noise pixels exactly."
msgstr ""
"最左側面板中是一個二值輸入區域：\n"
"一個實心方塊，中央有一個一像素的\n"
"孔洞，周圍有三個孤立的雜訊像素。\n"
"右側的四個面板顯示對該輸入套用\n"
"dilate、erode、open 與 close 的結果。\n"
"Dilate 擴張區域、填滿孔洞，並將每個\n"
"雜訊像素擴張成一塊；erode 收縮區域、\n"
"擴大孔洞，並移除雜訊；open 移除雜訊，\n"
"同時精確重現區域及其孔洞；close 填滿\n"
"孔洞，同時精確重現區域的輪廓與雜訊\n"
"像素。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/filters/morphology.rst:68
msgid ""
"The four classical morphological operations applied to a noisy binary "
"region. Erode shrinks; dilate grows; open is erode then dilate (removes "
"noise); close is dilate then erode (fills holes)."
msgstr ""
"對一個帶雜訊的二值區域套用四種經典形態學運算。Erode 收縮；dilate 擴張；open 是先 erode 後 dilate（移除雜訊）；close"
" 是先 dilate 後 erode（填滿孔洞）。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/filters/morphology.rst:74
msgid ""
":meth:`~image.Image.open` is *erode followed by dilate*. The eroded image "
"has had every isolated noise pixel removed, but it has also been shrunk by "
"``size`` pixels in every direction. Following the erode with a dilate of the"
" same size restores the genuine foreground regions to roughly their original"
" boundaries while leaving the noise gone. The composition is what makes "
"``open`` the standard \"remove noise\" operation in classical morphology: "
"isolated foreground pixels disappear, real regions come back unharmed."
msgstr ""
":meth:`~image.Image.open` 是 *先 erode 後 dilate*\\ 。經過 erode "
"的影像已移除所有孤立的雜訊像素，但同時也在每個方向上縮小了 ``size`` 個像素。在 erode 之後接上相同大小的 "
"dilate，可將真正的前景區域大致還原到原本的邊界，同時讓雜訊維持已被移除的狀態。正是這種組合讓 ``open`` "
"成為經典形態學中標準的「移除雜訊」運算：孤立的前景像素消失，而真正的區域則毫髮無傷地回復。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/filters/morphology.rst:87
msgid ""
":meth:`~image.Image.close` is the mirror image -- *dilate followed by "
"erode*. The dilate fills small holes inside foreground regions and connects "
"regions separated by small gaps; the erode shrinks the result back to its "
"original outer boundary while leaving the filled-in interior solid. "
"``close`` is the standard \"fill small gaps\" operation."
msgstr ""
":meth:`~image.Image.close` 是其鏡像——\\ *先 dilate 後 erode*\\ 。Dilate "
"填滿前景區域內部的小孔洞，並連接被小縫隙分開的區域；erode 則將結果收縮回原本的外部邊界，同時讓填補後的內部維持實心。\\ ``close`` "
"是標準的「填滿小縫隙」運算。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/filters/morphology.rst:101
msgid ""
"The size parameter has the same meaning as in the brightness filters: "
"``size=1`` means a 3-by-3 neighbourhood, ``size=2`` means 5-by-5, and so on."
" Larger sizes mean more aggressive cleanup -- and a longer per-pixel cost."
msgstr ""
"size 參數的意義與亮度濾波器中相同：\\ ``size=1`` 代表 3×3 的鄰域，\\ ``size=2`` 代表 5×5，依此類推。較大的 "
"size 代表更強烈的清理——以及更長的每像素成本。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/filters/morphology.rst:108
msgid "Top-hat and black-hat"
msgstr "頂帽與黑帽"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/filters/morphology.rst:110
msgid ""
"Two further compositions are worth knowing about because they extract "
"*exactly* the features that ``open`` and ``close`` remove:"
msgstr "另外兩種組合值得了解，因為它們擷取的 *正是* ``open`` 與 ``close`` 所移除的特徵："

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/filters/morphology.rst:114
msgid ""
":meth:`~image.Image.top_hat` returns the *difference* between the original "
"image and its opened version -- the foreground pixels that ``open`` would "
"have removed. That is literally a mask of the noise pixels, the isolated "
"small foreground regions, the thin foreground structures that the open "
"operation could not preserve. Useful for *extracting* small foreground "
"features when those features are the thing the application cares about, "
"rather than removing them."
msgstr ""
":meth:`~image.Image.top_hat` 回傳原始影像與其經 open 處理後版本之間的 *差異*\\ ——也就是 ``open`` "
"本來會移除的那些前景像素。這實際上就是一張遮罩，標示出雜訊像素、孤立的小型前景區域，以及 open "
"運算無法保留的細薄前景結構。當這些小型前景特徵正是應用程式所關心的對象，而非想要移除的目標時，這對於 *擷取* 它們很有用。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/filters/morphology.rst:126
msgid ""
":meth:`~image.Image.black_hat` returns the *difference* between the closed "
"version of the image and the original -- the background pixels that "
"``close`` would have filled in. That is a mask of the small holes inside "
"foreground regions, the narrow gaps between regions that the close operation"
" would have bridged."
msgstr ""
":meth:`~image.Image.black_hat` 回傳影像經 close 處理後版本與原始影像之間的 *差異*\\ ——也就是 "
"``close`` 本來會填補的那些背景像素。這是一張遮罩，標示出前景區域內部的小孔洞，以及 close 運算本來會橋接的區域間狹窄縫隙。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/filters/morphology.rst:135
msgid ""
"Both are less commonly reached for than the four basic operations, but the "
"pattern is worth remembering -- when an application needs to extract small "
"or thin features that the standard cleanup pass *removes*, the top-hat and "
"black-hat are the natural way to get them back."
msgstr ""
"這兩者都不如四種基本運算常用，但這個模式值得記住——當應用程式需要擷取標準清理流程所 *移除* "
"的小型或細薄特徵時，頂帽與黑帽正是把它們找回來的自然方法。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/filters/morphology.rst:144
msgid "Threshold mode"
msgstr "閾值模式"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/filters/morphology.rst:146
msgid ""
"The four basic morphological operations all accept an integer ``threshold`` "
"keyword that softens the on/off test at each position. Without it, the "
"operations behave the way the descriptions above said: "
":meth:`~image.Image.erode` requires *every* neighbour to be on, "
":meth:`~image.Image.dilate` requires *at least one*. With ``threshold`` set,"
" each operation tolerates that many neighbours voting the other way. For "
"erode, ``threshold`` is the number of *background* neighbours a pixel may "
"have and still survive: ``threshold=4`` keeps any pixel with at least four "
"of its eight neighbours on (in a 3-by-3 window the centre pixel has eight "
"neighbours), so it does not erode as aggressively. For dilate, ``threshold``"
" is the number of *foreground* neighbours a background pixel must have more "
"of before it turns on: ``threshold=2`` requires at least three foreground "
"neighbours instead of one, so it grows less aggressively."
msgstr ""
"四種基本形態學運算都接受一個整數 ``threshold`` 關鍵字，用來軟化每個位置的開/關測試。沒有它時，運算的行為如上述描述：\\ "
":meth:`~image.Image.erode` 要求 *每個* 鄰居都開啟，\\ :meth:`~image.Image.dilate` 則要求 "
"*至少有一個*\\ 。設定 ``threshold`` 後，每個運算可容忍那麼多個鄰居投下相反的票。對 erode 而言，\\ "
"``threshold`` 是一個像素可以擁有且仍能存活的 *背景* 鄰居數量：\\ ``threshold=4`` "
"會保留任何八個鄰居中至少有四個開啟的像素（在 3×3 視窗中，中心像素有八個鄰居），因此它的侵蝕沒那麼強烈。對 dilate 而言，\\ "
"``threshold`` 是一個背景像素必須多擁有的 *前景* 鄰居數量，才會被開啟：\\ ``threshold=2`` "
"要求至少有三個前景鄰居而非一個，因此它的擴張沒那麼強烈。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/image/filters/morphology.rst:169
msgid ""
"The threshold form is useful for tuning the aggressiveness of a "
"morphological pass without changing the size of its window, which would also"
" change the *scale* of features it acts on. Most applications stick with the"
" default behaviour; the threshold form is there for the cases where the "
"default is just slightly too much or too little."
msgstr ""
"閾值形式對於在不改變視窗大小的情況下調整形態學流程的強度很有用，因為改變視窗大小也會改變它所作用特徵的 *尺度*\\ "
"。大多數應用程式維持預設行為；閾值形式則是為了那些預設行為只是稍微太多或太少的情況而存在。"
